  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock id="Tag1624" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;1.&amp;#160; Not applicable.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock id="Tag1625" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;2.&amp;#160; Not applicable.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock id="Tag1626" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;3.&amp;#160; Not applicable.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock id="Tag1627" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;4.&amp;#160; Not applicable.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock id="Tag1628" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;5.&amp;#160; Not applicable.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="Tag1629" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;6.&amp;#160; TEC Trading, Inc. ("TEC&amp;#8221;) is owned by our member distribution cooperatives, and currently is our only Class&amp;#160;B member.&lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;We have a power sales contract with TEC, under which TEC purchases power from us that we do not need to meet the actual needs of our member distribution cooperatives and sells this power to the market under market-based rate authority granted by FERC.&lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;TEC also acquires natural gas and forward purchase contracts to hedge the price of natural gas to supply our combustion turbine facilities, and takes advantage of other power-related trading opportunities in the market which will help lower our member distribution cooperatives&amp;#8217; costs.&lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;TEC does not engage in speculative trading.&lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;To facilitate TEC&amp;#8217;s participation in the power-related markets, we have agreed to provide a maximum of $200.0 million in credit support to TEC.&lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;At December 31, 2025, we had issued $0.5 million in&amp;#160;guaranties for TEC.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 22.5pt;"&gt;We maintain a revolving credit facility to cover our short-term and medium-term funding needs that are not met by cash from operations or other available funds.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 22.5pt;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 22.5pt;"&gt;The $400 million in aggregate commitments under this credit agreement mature on December 7, 2028, unless earlier terminated in accordance with the agreement.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 22.5pt;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 22.5pt;"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, we did not have any borrowings outstanding under this facility; however the interest rate would have been 4.89%.&amp;#160; As of&amp;#160; December&amp;#160;31, 2024, we had outstanding under this facility $65.0 million in borrowings at a blended interest rate of 5.61%.&amp;#160; As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, we did not have any letters of credit outstanding under this facility.&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;On December 16, 2025, we issued $250 million of long-term debt in a private placement transaction.&amp;#160; The issuance consisted of $250 million of&amp;#160; First Mortgage Bonds, 2025 Series A due December 1, 2052 at an interest rate of 5.37%.&amp;#160; Commission authorization No. ES25-78-000.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="Tag1630" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;7.&amp;#160; On July 22, 2025, the Articles of Incorporation were amended to provide that amendments to&amp;#160;Old Dominion Electric Cooperative's Bylaws require a 2/3 majority vote, which gives legal effect to the requirement in the Bylaws that they can be amended only by 2/3 majority.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="Tag1631" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;8.&amp;#160; Not applicable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="Tag1632" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 12.0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;9.&lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Other than certain legal proceedings arising out of the ordinary course of business that management believes will not have a material adverse impact on our results of operations or financial condition, there is no other litigation pending or threatened against us.&lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock id="Tag1633" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 5.55pt; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; mso-layout-grid-align: none; punctuation-wrap: simple; text-autospace: none; mso-line-break-override: restrictions; margin: 0in 0in 0in 2.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;10.&amp;#160; Employment Agreement with President and Chief Executive Officer&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 5.55pt; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; mso-layout-grid-align: none; punctuation-wrap: simple; text-autospace: none; mso-line-break-override: restrictions; margin: 0in 0in 0in 2.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 5.55pt; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; mso-layout-grid-align: none; punctuation-wrap: simple; text-autospace: none; mso-line-break-override: restrictions; margin: 0in 0in 0in 2.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 101%; mso-layout-grid-align: none; punctuation-wrap: simple; text-autospace: none; mso-line-break-override: restrictions; margin: 1.95pt 6.55pt 0in 2.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 101%; mso-layout-grid-align: none; punctuation-wrap: simple; text-autospace: none; mso-line-break-override: restrictions; margin: 1.95pt 6.55pt 0in 2.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Old Dominion Electric&amp;#160;Cooperative's&amp;#160;(&amp;#8220;ODEC&amp;#8221;) board of directors appointed Christopher F. Cosby as President and Chief Executive Officer of ODEC, effective February 1, 2025.&amp;#160; On December 10, 2024, ODEC entered into an employment agreement with Mr. Cosby with an effective date of February 1, 2025.&amp;#160; The employment agreement is for a term of three years.&amp;#160; The agreement provides that he will receive an annual base salary of $1,150,000, effective as of February 1, 2025.&amp;#160; Salary increases shall be considered at each year end and may be awarded at the discretion of the board of directors.&amp;#160; Additionally, Mr. Cosby will be provided a $1,500 monthly automobile allowance.&amp;#160; Mr. Cosby is also entitled to participate in all benefit plans available to the employees of ODEC.&amp;#160; Under the agreement, if Mr. Cosby voluntarily terminates his employment following a material breach by ODEC or ODEC terminates his employment without specified cause, ODEC will pay Mr. Cosby compensation at the rate in effect on the date of termination for one additional year from the date of termination, plus medical insurance benefits, with limited exceptions.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 101%; mso-layout-grid-align: none; punctuation-wrap: simple; text-autospace: none; mso-line-break-override: restrictions; margin: 1.95pt 6.55pt 0in 2.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantChangesRelatedToRespondentCompanyAppearingInAnnualReportToStockholdersTextBlock id="Tag1634" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;12.&amp;#160; Not applicable.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantChangesRelatedToRespondentCompanyAppearingInAnnualReportToStockholdersTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="Tag1635" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;13.&amp;#160; See the following changes:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;On February 25, 2025, E. Garrison Drummond&amp;#160;notified us that he would resign from the board of directors of ODEC, effective as of February 25, 2025.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;On March 18, 2025, our board of directors elected Russell G. Brown as a member of the board of directors, effective March 18, 2025.&amp;#160; Mr. Brown was recommended to the nominating committee by Northern Neck Electric Cooperative.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;On March 18, 2025, our board of directors elected S. Keith Colonna&amp;#160;as a member of the board of directors, effective March 18, 2025.&amp;#160; Mr. Colonna&amp;#160;was recommended to the nominating committee by A&amp;amp;N Electric Cooperative.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;In connection with his resignation from Northern Neck Electric Cooperative, Bradley H. Hicks no longer meets the qualifications set forth in our Bylaws to serve as a member of our board of directors.&amp;#160; Effective April 16, 2025,&amp;#160; Mr. Hicks no longer serves as a member of the board of directors of ODEC.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;On May 13, 2025, our board of directors elected Richard E. McLendon&amp;#160;as a member of the board of directors, effective May 13, 2025.&amp;#160; Mr. McLendon&amp;#160;was recommended to the nominating committee by Northern Neck Electric Cooperative.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;In connection with his departure from Northern Neck Electric Cooperative, Mr. Russell G. Brown no longer meets the qualifications set forth in our Bylaws to serve as a member of our board of directors.&amp;#160; Effective September 18, 2025, Mr. Russell G. Brown no longer serves as a member of our board of directors.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;On December 9, 2025, our board of directors elected James A. Wise as a member of the board of directors, effective December 9, 2025.&amp;#160; Mr. Wise was recommended to the nominating committee by Northern Neck&amp;#160;Electric Cooperative.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;On December 18, 2025, Michael C. Wise was promoted to the position of Senior Vice President and Chief Operating Officer, effective January 1, 2026.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock id="Tag1636" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;14. We do have a cash management program and under CFR141.500(a) we were required to file an agreement with the Commission; however, since we are an electric cooperative, we are exempt from CFR141.500(c). &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock>
